From: Roman Rikhter <teledurak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw89: align the bus part of the TX skb control block

The bus keeps its part of the TX control block in hci_priv[] of struct
rtw89_tx_skb_data: for PCI, the DMA address of the frame and the mapping
of a frame sent from several buffers. hci_priv follows a pointer and two
u8, so it starts at offset 6 on 32-bit systems, and every access to the
DMA address and the mapping is misaligned. CPUs that don't handle
misaligned accesses trap on each of them, and the kernel emulates the
access: a frame takes four such traps on its way through the PCI bus,
seven if it is sent from several buffers. On an RTL8197F (MIPS 24Kc)
routing 230 Mbit/s to a station, the emulation took 0.5 % of the CPU.

Align hci_priv to 8 bytes, which also suits a 64-bit dma_addr_t on a
32-bit system. The PCI part then ends at 16 bytes on 32-bit systems and
at 32 bytes on 64-bit ones, within the 40 bytes of driver_data.

Signed-off-by: Roman Rikhter <teledurak@gmail.com>
---
diff --git drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.h drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.h
index ac997dd..dc1edfb 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.h
@@ -3671,7 +3671,7 @@ struct rtw89_tx_skb_data {
 	struct rtw89_tx_wait_info __rcu *wait;
 	u8 tx_rpt_sn;
 	u8 tx_pkt_cnt_lmt;
-	u8 hci_priv[];
+	u8 hci_priv[] __aligned(8);
 };
 
 #define RTW89_SCAN_NULL_TIMEOUT 30
